# Where tools/transcribe/bucket pushes and pulls training sets (docs/TRAINING-DATA.md). Copy to training.env (ignored
# by git) and fill in: an S3-compatible service and a key for that one bucket only. For a second one (a local S3
# server): training.local.env, used with TRAINING_ENV=training.local.env. The AWS tool runs in Docker, so a server
# on this machine is http://host.docker.internal:<port>, not localhost.
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_BUCKET=
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3_REGION=auto
